From 8e27f82653de1c219d9b1d97ab9af9a44ec8ee35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kuan-Jui Chiu <kchiu@axiado.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ax-ultra CMakeLists: limit -ffreestanding to C and ASM only

bali_hal/platform/ax-ultra/CMakeLists.txt adds -ffreestanding to
bali-hal-impl target options. GCC 13 arm-none-eabi in -ffreestanding C++
mode no longer exposes malloc/free. Restrict the flag to C/ASM only using
a CMake generator expression, matching the fix in base/r52-compile-args.cmake.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [GCC 13 toolchain compatibility fix]
Signed-off-by: Kuan-Jui Chiu <kchiu@axiado.com>
---
 platform/ax-ultra/CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/platform/ax-ultra/CMakeLists.txt b/platform/ax-ultra/CMakeLists.txt
index 4a5aadb..67dfe53 100644
--- a/platform/ax-ultra/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/platform/ax-ultra/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -78,7 +78,7 @@ target_compile_options(bali-hal-impl PRIVATE
     -nostartfiles
     -g
 	-nostdlib
-    -ffreestanding
+    "$<$<NOT:$<COMPILE_LANGUAGE:CXX>>:-ffreestanding>"
     -marm
     -mfloat-abi=hard
     -mfpu=neon-fp-armv8
-- 
2.34.1

